# The code spine of the graph-reading path (v0.11, code domain).
#
# Every base case here is a REAL symbol in the constellation's own source,
# resolved against a kannaka-memory code graph. Run it with --code-index and
# --unresolved strict and it becomes a structural pre-flight check: if a piece
# of the path is deleted, renamed, or left with nothing calling it, the build
# fails and names what went missing.
#
#   kannaka-hdl grow examples/code-spine.khdl \
#       --code-index ~/graphify-corpus/graph-index.sqlite --unresolved strict
#
# The spine spans two repositories, which is what `material` is for: the graph
# is found in kannaka-memory and read by a citizen in rogue-agent.
#
# The floors are the point:
#
#   min_persistence      how load-bearing the symbol is, from its in-degree.
#                        0.3 means "at least one thing calls it" — a spine
#                        part nothing calls is not a spine part any more.
#   min_noise_tolerance  the share of its edges graphify read straight from
#                        the source rather than inferring. 0.9 keeps the gate
#                        on facts, not on the graph's own guesses.
#
# Two honest limits, worth knowing before you trust a plan like this:
#
#   * A bare name can be ambiguous inside one repository. `norm` in
#     kannaka-memory is both a Python helper and a Rust function, and the
#     provider answers with the most load-bearing of them. Name spine parts
#     that are unique, or read the resolved file:line in the plan and check.
#   * Evidence-ladder and capability floors are refused outright here: code
#     carries no crystal evidence ladder and no behavioural contracts, and a
#     floor that cannot be evaluated must never be silently satisfied.

cell Spine() {
    when always => split Finding(), Reading()
}

# Finding the right subgraph for a question (kannaka-memory).
cell Finding() {
    when always => split Identifiers(), Lookup()
}

# Pulling the code-shaped names out of a plain question.
cell Identifiers() {
    when always => base code.symbol "identifiers" material "kannaka-memory" min_persistence 0.3 min_noise_tolerance 0.9
}

# Matching them against the graph and rendering the neighbourhood.
cell Lookup() {
    when always => base code.symbol "lookup" material "kannaka-memory" min_persistence 0.3 min_noise_tolerance 0.9
}

# The citizen that asks for the excerpt and answers from it (rogue-agent).
cell Reading() {
    when always => base code.symbol "graph_context" material "rogue-agent" min_persistence 0.3 min_noise_tolerance 0.9
}

grow Spine()

expect unresolved_components == 0
expect capacity >= 3
expect noise_tolerance > 0.85
